# GitHub Pages on a free account requires a PUBLIC repo, so anything committed
# here is world-readable. The plaintext idea list therefore stays out of git —
# only the encrypted public/ideas.sealed.json is committed, which is what makes
# the access code meaningful. Keep your own copy locally.
#
# The pattern is deliberately loose, because the name keeps changing: an
# ideas2.json once sat here untracked, and the list that replaced it arrived
# with invisible bidi marks in front of its name, which a plain `ideas*.json`
# does not match. Either one would have been published by the next `git add -A`.
*ideas*.json
!public/ideas.sealed.json

# Brand key visual — the design source, not needed to build.
FLY.png
.vite

# Design source for the hackathon page (a ~1 MB single-file HTML). Its icons,
# backgrounds and team colours were extracted into src/hackathon/assets.
new/
